      "content": "i hear what you're saying, but calling it \"morally bankrupt\" seems like you're totally dismissing the other side instead of actually looking at it. if someone commits a serious crime, isn't there a moral duty to the victim to ensure there's a proportional consequence? why is that view considered \"weak\" or \"flawed\" in your eyes?",
